C03: the Steam library title matches through punctuation and the English consequence is the observed state (INSTALL1621)

INSTALL1619 measured two remaining composer vetoes on truthful library finals: the model wrote «Batman: Arkham Knight» for the title «batman arkham knight» and the title check demanded the words contiguous (missing_name); the English draft «Stardew Valley is not in your Steam library, so it cannot be downloaded or installed» hit the failure lens because the mask covered «cannot download» but not «cannot be downloaded» (asserted_failure). For a verified game.entitlement.named result the title now matches through punctuation between its words, and the mask admits the English passive and the Spanish reflexive forms (descargarse, instalarse, desinstalarse).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


